 season's seasonal demand peak falling in Q1, not Q2, though this project cannot confirm that directly from the filing. Two things ate into YoY growth: finance costs rose 24.5% YoY (higher borrowings), and tax expense jumped 44.6% YoY -- together more than offsetting the 17.8% operating-profit gain. Company-level (standalone parent) PAT tells a very different story: up 84.4% YoY (LKR 1.294bn to LKR 2.386bn), driven almost entirely by a 97% jump in dividend income received from subsidiaries (LKR 1.05bn to LKR 2.07bn) -- income that eliminates on consolidation and so doesn't appear at all in the Group figures above. The Group view is the more representative one for the underlying trading business; the Company view mostly reflects subsidiary dividend timing.", "source_doc_id": "52077", "source_page": 1, "gaps_note": "QoQ and YoY both now use actual filed interim reports for every period (Q1 2025, Q2 2025, Q1 2026, Q2 2026) -- one report per as-of-date, no re-extraction of a period from a second/audited filing. The seasonal explanation for the QoQ swing is this project's inference, not something the filing itself states.", "takeaway": "CCS's steep QoQ drop looks alarming in isolation but is most likely New Year seasonality working in reverse; the more meaningful read is the YoY margin pressure from rising finance costs and tax, not a demand problem.", "qoq": [{"metric": "revenue", "label": "Revenue", "prior_period_label": "Q1 2026 (quarter ended 31 March 2026)", "prior_value": 50316475.0, "new_period_label": "Q2 2026 (quarter ended 30 June 2026)", "new_value": 50783209.0, "pct_change": 0.009275967762050103, "direction": "improved", "prior_period_end_date": "2026-03-31", "new_period_end_date": "2026-06-30"}, {"metric": "gross_profit", "label": "Gross Profit", "prior_period_label": "Q1 2026 (quarter ended 31 March 2026)", "prior_value": 7863698.0, "new_period_label": "Q2 2026 (quarter ended 30 June 2026)", "new_value": 6613405.0, "pct_change": -0.15899555145683367, "direc